@startuml
title Current WES Gateway deployment
actor "WES client" as client
rectangle "Helm release: wes-gateway" {
  component "Service :8090" as service
  component "Deployment\nUvicorn + FastAPI\nwes_api_gateway.main:app" as gateway
  artifact "Backend ConfigMap" as config
  database "Gateway run/artifact records\nSQLite PVC (default)" as records
}
rectangle "Toil bootstrap (separate deployment)" {
  component "Toil WES\ntenant-a" as a
  component "Toil WES\ntenant-b" as b
  component "Celery + Kubernetes execution" as execution
  database "Workflow storage" as storage
}
client --> service : /wes/v1/{namespace}
service --> gateway
gateway --> config : load registry at startup
gateway --> records : persist namespace and original backend
gateway --> a : WES HTTP requests
gateway --> b : WES HTTP requests
a --> execution
b --> execution
execution --> storage
note bottom of gateway
No built-in JWT validation or identity-based RBAC.
Other WES services can be configured in the registry.
PostgreSQL is supported as an alternative metadata store.
end note
@enduml
